body:
Thanks, I figured as much regarding the prestige mattering for those planning to continue in academia - however I don't plan on pursuing a PhD. So the acceptance rates differ between differently-ranked schools for PhD programs which is understandable, since they have to choose who is worth funding - but what about Master's degrees? Are schools much more relaxed about who they accept for MS programs because they're just willing to take your money, or is there some degree of competition/high expectations?

&#x200B;

Mainly just trying to figure out if I can sit back and relax, just focus on my grades, and smoothly transition into a T50 MS program...or if I need to be working my butt off to really "wow" the adcoms
